Alembic migrations for the planner database.

- env.py takes the database address from the planner's settings: DATABASE_URL in .env, or data/planner.db.
  It renders SQLite changes in batch mode, because SQLite cannot alter most columns in place.
- versions/0001_baseline.py creates the 16 tables. Later changes are added as new files in versions/.
- script.py.mako is the template Alembic uses when it writes a new migration file.

The planner applies these migrations every time it starts. To add one, follow "Adding a change to the schema"
in database/README.md.
